-- REGRESSION: fixed in the compiler retested on 2026-09-22. This generated host
-- now passes on wgpu 27 / Vulkan unchanged. Original failure documented below.
--
-- ORIGINAL BUG: the generated Rust bind-group layout uses pipeline-wide storage access
-- instead of the access declared by the SPIR-V entry point being instantiated.
--
-- Reproduce from this file's directory:
-- wyn build -O --target-double rust-wgpu --target spirv rust_host_storage_access_mismatch.wyn -o storage_access.spv
-- Include storage_access.rs as a Rust module using wgpu 27 with its spirv feature,
-- create let mut host = HostContext::new(&device)?, then call
-- host_reproduce(&mut host, &queue). No input resources are required.
--
-- EXPECTED: all filter phases have layouts matching their shader declarations;
-- the call completes and returns the compacted multiples of three.
-- BEFORE THE FIX: create_compute_pipeline for reproduce_local_offsets fails at group 0,
-- binding 2. Rust emits Storage { read_only: false }, while that SPIR-V stage's
-- storage declaration is read-only. wgpu reports:
-- "Storage class Storage { access: StorageAccess(LOAD | STORE) } doesn't match
-- the shader Storage { access: StorageAccess(LOAD) }".
--
-- The scratch buffer is written by an earlier phase and read by local_offsets.
-- Its pipeline-wide access union cannot specify the layout of each physical
-- stage: wgpu checks the shader's actual storage declaration. Wyn's rust_layout
-- currently filters bindings by stage but passes their pipeline-wide access to
-- binding_type unchanged. The layout must agree with the selected shader ABI.
--
-- CONTROL: compile the same source with --target wgsl and -o storage_access.wgsl.
-- That generated host call completes successfully. Failure (SPIR-V) and passing
-- control (WGSL) were both confirmed with wgpu 27 / Vulkan on 2026-09-22.
entry reproduce() []i32 =
  filter(|i| i % 3i32 == 0i32, iota(128i32))
